   "slug": "a-north-balcony-that-keeps-ferns-now",
   "title": "A north balcony that keeps ferns now",
   "date": "2026-10-20",
   "categories": [
    "notes"
   ],
   "tags": [],
   "image": "assets/images/c2.webp",
   "excerpt": "A north-facing balcony gets no direct sun, which is exactly what ferns want.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A north-facing balcony gets no direct sun, which is exactly what ferns want. We planted one at the nursery last year to see how it held up.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The ferns sat in grey pots against the wall and were watered twice a week. By the first frost they were fuller than when they arrived.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  },
  {
   "slug": "herbs-on-a-kitchen-sill-three-winters-on",
   "title": "Herbs on a kitchen sill, three winters on",
   "date": "2026-10-12",
   "categories": [
    "notes"
   ],
   "tags": [],
   "image": "assets/images/p1.webp",
   "excerpt": "A basil, thyme and parsley trio that has outlasted three winters.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Thyme and parsley carry on through winter on a bright sill. Basil does not, and we say so at the counter.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Keep the pots out of draughts, water in the morning, and pinch the tips often.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  },
  {
   "slug": "one-hydrangea-for-a-shaded-front-yard",
   "title": "One hydrangea for a shaded front yard",
   "date": "2026-10-03",
   "categories": [
    "notes"
   ],
   "tags": [],
   "image": "assets/images/p3.webp",
   "excerpt": "A single panicle hydrangea can carry a shaded front yard.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Panicle hydrangeas flower on new wood, so a hard prune in late winter is forgiven. They suit part shade and ordinary soil.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Plant it while the ground is still warm and mulch the first winter.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  }
